  "gaps": [
    "The capture contains several programs (B.S. Health Care Administration, M.S. Health Care Administration, and a partial Master of Public Health); this ledger assumes the intended program is the B.S. Health Care Administration.",
    "Open electives are printed as a range of 24-42 credits; the ledger uses 42 (the no-concentration path, since 30 general education + 48 major + 42 = 120). The capture states that if the optional 18-credit Emergency Medical Services Concentration (EMS 2301, EMS 2302, EMS 3301, EMS 3302, EMS 3306, EMS 4303) is completed, only 24 credit hours of electives are required.",
    "The capture references 'degree program upper-level requirements' for electives but does not state the required number of upper-level credits.",
    "Course lists for the Social and Behavioral Sciences, Natural Sciences, Mathematics, History, and English Composition general education blocks are not included in the capture; only Humanities and Fine Arts Groups A and B are listed.",
    "No residency or institutional-credit requirements (courses that must be completed at Columbia Southern) are stated in the capture.",
    "No minimum GPA or grade requirements are stated in the capture."
